6" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sejo of Joseon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sejo was the seventh king of Joseon, ruling from 1455 to 1468.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sejong-the-great"><span class="enc-name">Sejong the Great</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sejong the Great was the fourth king of Joseon Korea, ruling from 1418 to 1450.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sekeletu"><span class="enc-name">Sekeletu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sekeletu was king of the Kololo on the upper Zambezi from 1851, succeeding his father Sebetwane.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sekgoma-i"><span class="enc-name">Sekgoma I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sekgoma I was chief of the Bangwato, a Tswana people of present-day central Botswana, for most of the period from the 1830s until 1875.</span></a></li></ul>
